<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="PowerPC:BE:64:default:default">
<!--
    kuna analysis (option aif): no gap-walk function starts inside the code of a
    sized PowerPC64 ELFv1 symbol, whose value is a descriptor in .opd.

    Twenty-five leaves open with std 4,-8(1); addis 5,3,1; addi 3,5,n.  The same
    three instructions occur inside sample, which a symbol in .dynsym sizes at 28
    bytes:
        0xeb8  cmpdi 3,0 / beq 0xed0 / nop
        0xec4  std 4,-8(1) / addis 5,3,1 / addi 3,5,7
        0xed0  blr
    The size was read as that of the bytes at the descriptor, so the gap walk
    named sub_ec4 and sample ended there without its result.

    These keep their starts: the routine behind sample that has no symbol (0xed4),
    inner, a symbol inside outer (0xef0), and the routine behind the 8 bytes of
    dotted (0xf24), whose symbol states its descriptor's 24 bytes as the dot-symbol
    ABI does.  kuna-cli's elfv1_entries covers a call target inside a function.

    Stage: P1 program prep (code/data partition), option aif (the drivers' default
    on every architecture but x86-64).  Single pass per byte order.

    Images: decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/
    elfv1_symbol_extent_be.so and elfv1_symbol_extent_le.so
    (elfv1_symbol_extent.S).
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">4e80002000000000</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/elfv1_symbol_extent_be.so</com>
  <com>option listing on</com>
  <com>option aif on</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>functions</com>
  <com>lo fu sample</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/elfv1_symbol_extent_le.so</com>
  <com>option listing on</com>
  <com>option aif on</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>functions</com>
  <com>lo fu sample</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="elfv1-symbolextent #1: sample is listed" min="2" max="2">0xeb8 sample</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="elfv1-symbolextent #2: no start inside sample" min="0" max="0">sub_ec4</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="elfv1-symbolextent #3: sample keeps its result" min="2" max="2">a0 \+= 0x10007;|return a0 \+ 0x10007;</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="elfv1-symbolextent #4: the routine behind sample is a start" min="2" max="2">0xed4 sub_ed4</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="elfv1-symbolextent #5: a symbol inside outer is a start" min="2" max="2">0xef0 inner</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="elfv1-symbolextent #6: a descriptor's own size bounds no code" min="2" max="2">0xf24 sub_f24</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
